       •   X/Open  Curses,  Issue  4,  Version 2 (1996), describes these func‐
           tions, marking them as “TO BE WITHDRAWN”.

       •   X/Open Curses, Issue 7 (2009) marks the  _t_e_r_m_c_a_p  interface  (along
           with vvwwpprriinnttww and vvwwssccaannww) as withdrawn.

       Neither X/Open Curses nor the SVr4 man pages documented the return val‐
       ues of ttggeetteenntt correctly, though all three shown here were in fact  re‐
       turned  ever  since  SVr1.   In  particular,  an omission in the X/Open
       Curses specification has been misinterpreted to mean that  ttggeetteenntt  re‐
       turns  OOKK or EERRRR.  Because the purpose of these functions is to provide
       compatibility with the _t_e_r_m_c_a_p library, that  is  a  defect  in  X/Open
       Curses, Issue 4, Version 2 rather than in _n_c_u_r_s_e_s.

